Write every node meowcaller sends from whatsmeow's event dispatch through one ordered queue, off the dispatch.

Origin: fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector, upstream meowcaller code (not from a pull request).

Why: patch 0014 moved the preaccept off the dispatch, and four writes were still made on it: the relaylatency responses, the deferred accept that a mute_v2 sends, the typed call-control acks and the video acks. whatsmeow's socket writes with the socket's own context, so any of them blocking on a socket that stopped draining held every node behind it, the account's messages and call terminations included, until the socket closed. A goroutine per write would let them overtake each other, and the order matters (preaccept, relaylatency, accept), so they go through sendLater: a FIFO drained by one goroutine that exists only while there is something to send.

The preaccept's goroutine from 0014 is replaced by the same queue, so it keeps its place ahead of the relaylatency responses.

